<!--
    A byte array in a SPARC V9 64-bit frame at stack 0x7f5..0x7f6 (bias
    0x7ff - 10) is passed to a call that may write it, then read back:

        unsigned char delim(unsigned char c) {
          unsigned char buf[1];  // fp+0x7f5
          buf[0] = c;
          mutate(buf);
          return buf[0];
        }

    SparcV9_64.cspec declares the hidden struct-return pointer as a stack
    entry at 0x7ef..0x7f6. Clearing that entry's storage out of the local
    range in a function with no hidden return dropped every local there:
    the address printed as an undeclared Stack location and the reload read
    the stale argument. Hand-assembled; mutate is a retl stub.

    Control: fill_raw has no prototype and reads its hidden return pointer
    from that slot (ldx [%fp+0x7ef]; stx 5 through it; return it). The read
    keeps the slot a parameter; released, the store went through an
    uninitialized local instead.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
9de3bf50f02fa7f59007a7f54000000d01000000f00fa7f581c7e00881e80000010000000100000001000000010000000100000001000000010000000100000081c3e00801000000
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100080" readonly="true">
9de3bf50c25fa7ef84102005c4704000b010000181c7e00881e80000
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="delim"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100040" name="mutate"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100080" name="fill_raw"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>map prototype mutate void mutate(unsigned char *p);</com>
  <com>lo fu delim</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu fill_raw</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
